# Emrakul, the Promised End: "This spell costs {1} less to cast for each card type among cards in your graveyard." Four cards reach Bot1's
# graveyard on turn 1: Tarfire (Kindred Instant), Haywire Mite (Artifact Creature) killed by it, Duress (Sorcery), and on turn 7 the sacrificed Black
# Lotus (Artifact again). That is five types - kindred, instant, artifact, creature, sorcery - from four cards (a card of two types counts both,
# a type twice counts once; the Lotus adds nothing): {13} less five is {8}. Bot2's graveyard holds an enchantment (Duress takes its Rancor), a type
# Bot1's lacks, and it does not count ("your graveyard"). Bot1 taps exactly eight mana (Mountain, two Islands, Mox Jet, Mox Pearl, Black Lotus
# {R}{R}{R}) and the pool is empty after the cast, so the discount is neither six nor four. The Emrakul that resolves has flying and trample.
# On turn 10 Deconstruction Hammer equipped to it gives "{3}, {T}, Sacrifice ...": an ability of Emrakul, not a spell, so the five types in the
# graveyard (the Hammer adds none) discount it by nothing and it costs exactly {3}: the pool is empty after paying three.

